    the title is "Old Age Security Act, as Blawx encodes it".
    the case is a scenario, with the documents it is stated in.
    the facts about "the case" are
        a person is a person,
        a person was a pensioner on July 1 1977,
        a person was born on a time,
        as of July 1977 a person resided in Canada,
        as of July 1977 a person possessed a valid immigration visa,
        as of July 1977 a person had resided in Canada after 18 years of age,
        a person resided in canada for 10 years prior to approval,
        a person was in Canada more than away between 18 and 10 years prior to approval,
        a person resided in Canada for the year prior to approval,
        a person resided in Canada at least 40 years since the age of 18,
        a person was a citizen or legal resident the day before approval.
    the result is the answer to query which_a_full_monthly_pension_may_be_paid_to.
    the result shows its reasons.
    the result shows its citations.
    the result can be flipped.

